The referenced `@id` doesn't exist anywhere — click the lens to see
the "(missing)" info toast surface:

- [ ] orphaned reference <!-- @id:m9dangle @parent:never-existed -->

### Navigation highlight (M10)

After clicking any forward-edge lens (the navigate ones, not the peek
ones), the target line stays softly tinted via the
`tsk.navigation.highlight` theme color until you do one of three
things: click another navigate lens (the highlight follows the next
jump), move the cursor with the keyboard or mouse, or switch to a
different editor. There's no fade timer — the highlight sticks around
so you can find your spot after scrolling, then clears itself the
moment you start interacting again. Override the tint via
`workbench.colorCustomizations` if the default soft yellow clashes
with your theme.

## Parser model (M2)

The parser reads every line above into a `Task` record exposing `marker`,
`indent`, `content`, an insertion-ordered `metadata` Map, a `tags` array, and
a zero-indexed `line`. Nothing visible yet — M3 plugs this into a SQLite cache
and surfaces it via commands — but the model is exercised by these examples.

